---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Anim from "../../components/Anim.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="@open-rgs/fill  - Frequency"
  description="Fill: Weighted draws, one cell at a time."
>
  <main>
    <p class="dim"><a href="/extension">&larr; extensions</a></p>
    <h1>@open-rgs/fill</h1>

    <p class="lede">Weighted draws, one cell at a time.</p>

    <Anim kind="fill" caption="Every cell drawn independently. <code>expectedCount</code> makes &quot;how many scatters per spin&quot; arithmetic rather than a simulation." />

    <p>This is the direct strip replacement, and it deliberately does NOT do adjacency - that belongs to markov, layered on top. Most balancing work is frequency work and should not require thinking about neighbours.</p>

    <h2 data-section="&sect;">Reach for</h2>
    <pre><code>{`import { ... } from "@open-rgs/fill";`}</code></pre>
    <p class="dim">fillWeights(shape, weights)  &middot;  fillWeightsPerColumn  &middot;  constant  &middot;  expectedCount</p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
